.TH INFRAGENIE 1 "August 2026" "v0.1.0" "InfraGenie Manual"
.SH NAME
infragenie \- Autonomous AI-Native DevSecOps Orchestrator
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B infragenie
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fICOMMAND\fR [\fIARGS\fR]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B InfraGenie
is an autonomous DevSecOps orchestrator that bridges application source code to a live, hardened production workload on AWS ECS Fargate. It performs AST semantic code analysis, AI-driven multi-stage Dockerfile generation adhering to CIS benchmarks, automated Trivy security vulnerability audits, and production AWS ECS Fargate container deployment.

.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Enable verbose debug logging output.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Display command-line help menu and exit.

.SH COMMANDS
.TP
\fBanalyze\fR [\fIPATH\fR] [\fB\-o\fR \fIFILE\fR]
Inspect project tech stack, language, framework, exposed ports, environment variables, and /health routes.
.TP
\fBgenerate\fR [\fIPATH\fR] [\fB\-d\fR] [\fB\-o\fR \fIDIR\fR]
Use LLM (Gemini, Claude, GPT, or Ollama) with RAG context to generate production-ready Dockerfile and .dockerignore.
.TP
\fBscan\fR [\fITARGET\fR] [\fB\-i\fR]
Run Trivy security scan on local project filesystem or built container image (-i).
.TP
\fBdeploy\fR [\fIPATH\fR] [\fB\-t\fR \fITAG\fR] [\fB\-c\fR \fICOUNT\fR]
Deploy container to AWS ECS Fargate via Amazon ECR repository. Builds and pushes Docker image to Amazon ECR.
.TP
\fBrun\fR [\fIPATH\fR] [\fB\-s\fR] [\fB\-d\fR]
Master 1-Click Pipeline: Execute Analyze -> Generate -> Scan -> Deploy sequentially.
.TP
\fBdoctor\fR
Run diagnostic health check on Python, AI keys, Docker, Trivy, and AWS credentials.
.TP
\fBrm\fR [\fIPATH_OR_NAME\fR] [\fB\-f\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-ecr\fR]
Remove deployed AWS cloud resources (ECS Fargate service, task definitions, and ECR repository).

.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Analyze current project directory:
.B infragenie analyze .
.TP
Generate Dockerfile preview (dry-run):
.B infragenie generate . -d
.TP
Run full pipeline skipping AWS deploy:
.B infragenie run . -s
.TP
Force delete AWS resources:
.B infragenie rm my-app -f

